---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const trail = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Affiliate Disclosure', href: '/affiliate-disclosure/' }];
---
<Page
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  eyebrow="Money"
  description="How Going Eagle makes money, what an affiliate link is, and the specific rules we follow so that commission never influences a recommendation."
  intro="Going Eagle uses affiliate links. Here is precisely what that means, what it costs you, and the rules we have set so it cannot bend our advice."
  trail={trail}
>
  <h2>The plain version</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you click one and buy something, the retailer
    pays us a small commission. <strong>You pay exactly the same price either way</strong> — the
    commission comes out of the retailer's margin, not your pocket.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is how this site is funded. There is no paywall, no subscription and no sponsored
    content, and we would rather be honest about the trade-off than pretend the content is free
    to produce.
  </p>

  <h2>What we will not do</h2>
  <p>These are commitments, not aspirations. If we break one, hold us to it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>We will not re-order a ranking for money.</strong> If the product paying us 3% is
      better than the one paying 10%, the 3% product goes first. Our
      <a href="/gear/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> is published so you can check our
      reasoning against our conclusions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We will not accept payment for a positive review.</strong> No brand can buy a score,
      a placement, or a favourable sentence on this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We will not hide the disclosure.</strong> It appears above the first affiliate link
      on the page, not only down here in the small print.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We will not replace a citation with an affiliate link.</strong> When a claim needs a
      source, it gets a source, even when there is a monetisable alternative.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We will not recommend a purchase you do not need.</strong> A significant number of
      pages here conclude that the reader should keep the equipment they own and spend the money
      on a lesson instead.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to spot an affiliate link</h2>
  <p>
    Affiliate links on this site are marked in the page's HTML with
    <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>, which is the standard signal search engines and browser
    tools use to identify them. Every page containing one carries a visible notice above the
    first instance.
  </p>

  <h2>Programs we participate in</h2>
  <p>
    We work with golf retailers and manufacturers through affiliate networks. As our program
    memberships are confirmed we will list them here by name, so you can see exactly who has a
    financial relationship with this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If anything about our commercial arrangements is unclear, ask.
    <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> and we will answer directly.
  </p>
</Page>
